# Which of the four absence reasons each question has ever taken. One row per absence-bearing
# question: its reasons as a four-bit word, and how many filings stand behind it.
#
# The split is a schema boundary
#   The rows are sorted so that the sites reaching `none` sit together and the ones that never do
#   sit together. The split is not cosmetic: it is the `pm:Absence` / `pm:ClaimAbsence` boundary,
#   printed from the data rather than read off the schema, and a site on the wrong side of it is a
#   defect.
#
# Sorted on the bit, not the string
#   A collation that files punctuation after letters buries the split this query exists to show,
#   so the `none` bit is pulled out and ordered explicitly.
-- §12  Every absence-bearing question as a four-bit word: n·u·a·d.
SELECT m.question       AS "question!",
       m.mask           AS "mask!",
       m.filings        AS "filings!",
       m.as_none        AS "as_none!"
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/state_masks.sqlc)
) m
ORDER BY (m.mask LIKE 'n%') DESC, m.filings DESC, m.question
